  Target:   holding/hooks/new-check.sh
  Category: D38_HOLDING_IMPL
  Detail:   LAYER=L0 forbidden on holding/{hooks,scripts,skills,commands,bin}/ — file should be at sutra/marketplace/plugin/<surface>/ or sutra/hooks/

  Rule:
    Implementation surfaces default to plugin L0. holding/{hooks,scripts,
    skills,commands,bin}/** requires explicit L1 or L2 justification.

  Required marker fields at .claude/build-layer-registered (multi-line KV):
    LAYER=L0|L1|L2
    SCOPE=fleet|cohort:<name>|single-instance:<name>
    TARGET_PATH=<abs path>
    WHY_NOT_L0_KIND=staging|instance-only       (L1/L2 only)
    WHY_NOT_L0_REASON=<non-empty>               (L1/L2 only)
    PROMOTE_TO=<plugin path>                    (L1 only, non-NONE)
    PROMOTE_BY=<YYYY-MM-DD>                     (L1 only, non-NONE)
    OWNER=<durable role>                        (L1 only, non-NONE)
    ACCEPTANCE=<non-empty>                      (L1 only, non-NONE)
    TS=<unix>

  Quick fixes:
    - If this is universal/generic, write to:
        sutra/marketplace/plugin/<surface>/        (Claude Code marketplace surfaces)
        sutra/hooks/                                (git/runtime universals)
    - If L1 staging: declare PROMOTE_TO + PROMOTE_BY + OWNER + ACCEPTANCE.
    - If L2 instance-only: declare WHY_NOT_L0_KIND=instance-only + non-empty WHY_NOT_L0_REASON.

  Override (one tool call, audit-logged):
    BUILD_LAYER_ACK=1 BUILD_LAYER_ACK_REASON='<specific-reason>' <tool>

